    "https://www.burmanu.ca/sites/default/files/Final%20-%20Education%20Job%20Advert%20-%20September%2016%2C%202026.pdf": {
      "title": "Job Title: Full-time Tenure-track Faculty Position in Education",
      "description": " \n \n \nJob Title: Full-time Tenure-track Faculty Position in Education  \nClassification: Salary \n(Range - Annual Salary: Assistant Professor to Associate Professor - $66,840.00 - \n$114,216.00) \nDepartment/School: School of Education \nAvailable: January 2027  \nPosition Overview: The Faculty of Education invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in \nCurriculum and Instruction. We are seeking an exceptional educator and scholar \ndedicated to high-quality teaching instruction for K-12 in Literacy Education, innovative \ninstructional design, and teacher preparation. The successful candidate will \ndemonstrate a strong commitment to evidence-based pedagogical practices, student \nmentorship, and active engagement in research and service. \nPrimary Responsibilities: \nTeaching & Instruction \n• Design and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Curriculum and \nInstruction, teaching methodology, and general education principles across \nin-person, online, and hybrid formats. \n• Model learner-centered, inclusive, and research-informed pedagogical \nstrategies. \n• Observe, evaluate, and mentor teacher candidates during field experiences \nand student teaching practicums. \n• Continuously update course content to reflect contemporary educational \nresearch, policy changes, and technological advances. \nScholarly Activity & Service \n• Maintain an active research program in curriculum theory, instructional \ndesign, or teacher education, contributing to peer-reviewed publications and \nacademic conferences. \n• Advise and mentor undergraduate students in their academic and \nprofessional development. \n• Serve on departmental, faculty, and university-level committees. \n• Build partnerships with local schools, districts, and community educational \norganizations. \nPosition Qualifications: The ideal candidate will hold an earned Ph.D. in Curriculum and Instruction (or \nclosely related field) by the start date, possess at least 3 years of K–12 classroom \nteaching experience, and demonstrate excellence in university teaching alongside \nan active research agenda. A demonstrated commitment to Seventh-day Adventist \neducation, community service, and research and writing for scholarly publications \nis required. \n \nAdditional preferred assets include: \nExperience with digital learning environments (e.g., Canvas, Blackboard). \nExperience supervising field placements or building school district partnerships. \nA record or promise of securing external research funding. \n \n\nApplication Materials \nRequired: \n \n \n \n \n \n \nInterested candidates should submit the following documents: \n• Cover Letter detailing interest in the position and qualifications. \n• Curriculum Vitae (CV) including educational background, teaching experience, \nand publication record. \n• Statement of Teaching Philosophy (2 pages max) highlighting pedagogical \napproaches, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and student engagement \nstrategies. \n• Statement of Research Interests (2 pages max). \n• Contact Information for Three Professional References (including at least one \nwho can directly address teaching quality). \n• Sample student evaluations \n \nContact: Dr. Chloe Weir, Vice President for Academic Administration \n6730 University Drive Lacombe, AB T4L 2E5 Canada  \nTelephone: 403-782-3381, Extension 4031  \nEmail: chloeweir@burmanu.ca \n "
    }
